.TH "REPROCTL\-DOWN" "1" "2026" "reproctl" "Repro Development Tools"
.SH NAME
reproctl\-down \- stop all services and optionally tear down the cluster
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]reproctl\f[R] [\f[B]\-\-json\f[R]] \f[B]down\f[R]
[\f[B]\-\-cluster\f[R]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Stop all running services by tearing down the Tilt daemon.
This is equivalent to \f[B]reproctl stop \-\-all\f[R].
.PP
By default, the kind cluster is left running so that a subsequent
\f[B]reproctl up\f[R] can start quickly.
Use \f[B]\-\-cluster\f[R] to also remove the cluster and container
registry.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\f[B]\-\-cluster\f[R]
Also tear down the kind cluster and container registry after stopping
services.
.TP
\f[B]\-\-json\f[R]
Output a JSON summary of the operation.
The object includes the command name and whether the cluster was
removed.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
reproctl down
Stop all services, leave cluster running.
.TP
reproctl down \-\-cluster
Stop all services and tear down the cluster.
.TP
reproctl \-\-json down
Stop all services and output JSON summary.
.SH SEE ALSO
\f[B]reproctl\f[R](1), \f[B]reproctl\-up\f[R](1),
\f[B]reproctl\-stop\f[R](1), \f[B]reproctl\-cluster\f[R](1)
.SH AUTHORS
